{"id":"r01","type":"research","question":"What did the 2015 Open Science Collaboration replication project in psychology find?","rubric":["States that about 100 studies were replicated","States that roughly 36% (about a third) of replications had statistically significant results","Notes that replication effect sizes were about half of the originals","Cites a specific publication (journal, year or URL), not just the project name"]}
{"id":"r02","type":"research","question":"Does chain-of-thought prompting help small language models?","rubric":["Says the benefit of chain-of-thought depends on model scale","Mentions that the original chain-of-thought results found gains mainly in large models (around 100B parameters)","Notes newer evidence that small models can benefit when trained or fine-tuned for reasoning (for example distillation)","Cites at least one specific paper (title, authors and year, or URL)"]}
